  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "Preamble – Effective agreement and collaboration",
    "text": "This Agreement, effective upon signing, governs an arrangement whereby Dr, Dario Campana of St. Jude Children's Research Hospital, inc e (\"St. Jude\") agrees to provide biological material that is proprietary to St. Jude, for use In a collaborative research study with Dr. Carl June (\"Recipient Scientist') of th University of Pennsylvania (\"Recipient\"), subject to the terms and conditions set forth below."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "Section 1 — Definition of Material",
    "text": "1. The biological material to be provided to Recipient Scientist is the anti-CD19-BB-.; chirnerio T-eell receptor construct, Including any progeny, portions, unmodified derivatives and any accompanying know-how or data ('Material\")."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "2. Permitted users and custody",
    "text": "2. The Material is for use by Recipient Scientist or persone dIrectly supervised by Recipient Scientist. The Material may net be transferred or taken to any ether laboratory or made available to any other person or third party, but is to remain under the immediate and direct control of Redplent Scientist."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "3. Permitted research use",
    "text": "3. Recipient Scientist agrees that the Material will only be used to create a lentiviral chimeric, T-cell receptor construct to be used in pre-clinical studies."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "4. Human and commercial use restrictions",
    "text": "4. The Material may not be used in humans and will be stored, used, and disposed of in accordance with applicable law and regulations, The Material will not be used for any commercial purpose."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "5. Distribution rights",
    "text": "5. St. Jude retains the unresteicted rig ht to distribute the Material to other commercial or noncommercial entities."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "6. Joint publication",
    "text": "6. Recipient agrees that any publications that result from the collaborative research study between St. Jude and Recipient Scientist using the Material be jointly published in accordance with academic standards."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "7. Rights, termination, and destruction",
    "text": "7. The transfer of the Material grants te Recipient no rights In the Material other than those specifically set forth in the Agreement. Thls agreement may be terminated • upon thirty (30) clays written notice by either party to the other. Upon termination of 332 N,34-t1 Liwddnk Stre\". mcinoli::. TN .1 ,3105 2 .7 '.)4 I 1901 .49;! . .DIM Iwww.Ykitorl,'. 1 2 • the agreement, Recipient shall destroyall unused Materials."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "Section 8 — Commercialization approval",
    "text": "a. Recipient shall not commercialize any product that contains Material without the prior written approval of St. Jude."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "9. Disclaimer of warranties",
    "text": "9. The Material provided is experimental in nature, and it Is provided WITHOUT ANY i14 11 WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FORA PARTICULAR USE. / St. Jude MAKES NO REPRESENTATION AND PROVIDES NO WARRANTYTHAT THE USE OF THE MATERIAL WILL NOT iNFRINGE ANY PATENT OR OTHER PROPRIEJARYBIGHT--."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "10. Liability limitation",
    "text": "10. Except to the extent prohibited by taw, the Recipient assumes all Rability for damages that may arise from its use, storage or disposal of the Materials. St. Jude and corporate affiliates of St. Jude and their respective boards of Governors, Directors, officers. staff, representatives and agents will not be Uableto the Recipient for any damages, expenses (Including without limitation legai expenses), losses, claims, demands, suit brother actions (colleottvely hereinafter nelaims\") made by the Recipient, or made against the Recipient byany other party, due to or arising from the use, storage or disposal of the Materials by the Recipient, except to the odent such Claims are solely caused by the gross negligence or willful misconduct of St. Jude."
  }
]

